      "text": "Make several sweeping AND several detail edits to this collection's pack.json - not one small tweak. SWEEPING edits (at least 3): change the large-scale composition - silhouettes, mass distribution, landmark hierarchy and value/colour contrast across the scene; for example reshape or add large masses, spans, voids, ceiling teeth or banding with feature-scale rectangles, and consolidate the busy centre around the breach so the paired broken register faces read as the dominant focal cue. DETAIL edits (at least 8): add meso/micro craft - seams, scars, joints, rust, cable and rail marks, strata variation, restrained bright accents; group the near-continuous thin orange deck-edge marks into a few purposeful damaged or instrumented sections. Start from the problems your own image critique found. Work in batches: after each batch run the validator, and fix or undo anything that fails. When the edits are done, regenerate the preview (render_write), run render_check, re-render with Godot (render_capture), compare_captures, and view the new image before you report. Keep every feature inside its documented bounds and reusable. In your report state honestly which edits helped, which regressed or added noise, and whether the after image is better than the before image."
